cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the M-ABSA benchmark. Paper publication details will be added after acceptance."
title: "Memory-Efficient Cross-Lingual and Cross-Domain Aspect-Based Sentiment Analysis of E-Commerce Reviews"
abstract: >-
  Experiment code for English-only ABSA on M-ABSA. Includes frozen Qwen
  prompting, three-seed Qwen and mT5 comparisons, Laptop UABSA Gemma
  adaptation, empty-label review loss weighting, and frozen domain transfer.
  Primary results use raw exact-tuple micro-F1 with an explicit blank-TASD rule.
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mzain4/crosslingual-absa-qwen3"
keywords:
  - aspect-based sentiment analysis
  - cross-lingual transfer
  - few-shot prompting
  - QLoRA
  - parameter-efficient fine-tuning
  - large language models
  - M-ABSA
